--TEST--
An enum constant may not reuse a case's name, because `Name::X` reads both, and an enum method may not use `yield`, because a case is an integer and a generator keeps its receiver in an object — `rule:enums/an-enum-body-takes-methods-and-constants`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Grade {
    A,
    B,

    public const int A = 3;

    public function steps(): Iterator<int> {
        yield $this as int;
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0304]: the enum `Grade` declares `A` as a case and as a constant
%A
error[E0220]: an enum method cannot use `yield`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
